    "body": "Addresses https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/35118#discussion_r3514230802.\r\n\r\n`ConsumeUniValue` isn't that useful as a shared fuzz helper, as it just returns the same hard-coded fields. This PR removes it and updates the `ipc` target to read a UniValue directly from fuzzer input instead. This is similar to what the `parse_univalue` target already does, and lets `ipc` test with different JSON values instead of one fixed value.",
